# Kotlin & Jetpack Compose Guidelines

## Compose Best Practices
- Use `@Composable` annotation for all UI functions
- Follow the naming convention: `ScreenName` for screens, `ComponentName` for reusable components
- Use `Modifier` parameter with default value for all composables
- Implement proper state management with `StateFlow` and `collectAsState()`

## ViewModel Guidelines
- Extend `ViewModel` class for all ViewModels
- Use `MutableStateFlow` for internal state, expose `StateFlow` for UI
- Handle data loading states (loading, success, error)
- Use `viewModelScope` for coroutines

## Data Classes
- Use `@Serializable` annotation for API models
- Implement helper functions in data classes for display formatting
- Follow naming conventions: `Pet`, `PetCareCenter`, `User`

## File Organization
- Keep composables in separate files by feature
- Group related components in the same package
- Use descriptive file names that match the component name

## State Management
- Use `remember` and `mutableStateOf` for local UI state
- Use ViewModels for business logic and data state
- Implement proper error handling and loading states

